{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 as an operational internal time source for the cluster.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 ran enabled chrony, permitted node2, listened on UDP/123, and remained synchronized to its upstream source. Node2's successful use of 10.100.45.10 directly confirms that node1 served time.","evidence_ids":["cmd-897185b397f54a01","cmd-1d4ab1918d504f05","cmd-b8eb0227341e4883"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure node2 to synchronize exclusively against node1 rather than a public time server.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2's sole configured source was 10.100.45.10. Chrony selected it as the active source, reported it as the reference ID, and reached normal synchronized status before and after the restart sequence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2e78514554ec4af9","cmd-bacd6915cab64220","cmd-b8eb0227341e4883"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Required package installation, time-service configuration, service restarts, and node reboots had clear roles. One unnecessary mutation occurred: cmd-54743c005ccc4115 started a tcpdump capture and created /tmp/ntp-capture.log and /tmp/ntp-capture.pid, but no later command inspected the capture or used it to produce the recovery; both files remained after execution. The capture process itself was bounded by timeout, but its file residue was not cleaned. No failed services or package damage were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-54743c005ccc4115","cmd-bacd6915cab64220","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered chrony/configuration state. Node2 was initially unsynchronized immediately after its reboot, but a chrony restart restored synchronization and the final state was healthy.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor listening-socket snapshot for node1 was blank despite the terminal evidence showing UDP/123 listening shortly beforehand. Node2's final synchronization directly against node1 substantially mitigates this collector inconsistency.","The tcpdump capture contents were never collected, so they provide no evidence and their sensitivity cannot be assessed."]}
